From 34c1d4f67c1ff04ea94a9641f8f4a830f2c506a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 16:37:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 327/638] content: apply CEF content_main_654986 (split
 ContentMain lifecycle)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fold cef/patch/patches/content_main_654986.patch so libcef_static links.
CEF's main_runner.cc drives the ContentMain lifecycle in separate stages, but
content only exposed the monolithic RunContentProcess(). This splits it:

- content/app/content_main.cc: extract ContentMainInitialize / ContentMainRun /
  ContentMainShutdown from RunContentProcess(), which now composes them.
- content/public/app/content_main.h: CONTENT_EXPORT decls for the three stages.
- content/app/content_main_runner_impl.{h,cc}: add ShutdownOnUIThread()
  (resets discardable_shared_memory_manager_ under a ScopedAllowBaseSync guard);
  mark ContentMainRunnerImpl CONTENT_EXPORT so CEF can hold it directly.
- base/process/set_process_title.cc: drop the CurrentId()==getpid() DCHECK per
  the CEF patch.

Resolves the four undefined symbols in build 19 (main_runner.cc:309/429/452/479/563):
content::ContentMainInitialize/Run/Shutdown + ContentMainRunnerImpl::ShutdownOnUIThread.
Applied verbatim at -p0 on top of the AROS startup-telemetry checkpoint
4658c88d8e (my telemetry breadcrumbs preserved). NOTE: the patch's unconditional
base/threading/thread_restrictions.h include coexists with an existing
IS_IOS-guarded one — benign (header-guarded, iOS-only) and kept faithful to the
upstream CEF patch for rebaseability.

Completes codex; codex validates the libcef_static link.

